            {
                "entry_id": "ab3a14b4-ad67-34fa-b670-1cbac7d84385",
                "word": "mooring",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6050fc77-e08b-417e-a08a-d1269deb465c",
                        "entry_id": "ab3a14b4-ad67-34fa-b670-1cbac7d84385",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "moorings"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "081f8fd9-3c03-3f3a-ab68-653f9a28abce",
                        "entry_id": "ab3a14b4-ad67-34fa-b670-1cbac7d84385",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A place to moor a vessel."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "15a3bab4-8b68-4f0e-b24e-b5a3c2693a6a",
                                "sense_id": "081f8fd9-3c03-3f3a-ab68-653f9a28abce",
                                "text": "Then did the comet break loose from his moorings and the eclipse roamed about the sky, and down on the earth did Death’s three children—Famine, Pestilence, and Drought—come out to feed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "560b159e-f395-44af-b1c5-382a9846dbac",
                                "sense_id": "081f8fd9-3c03-3f3a-ab68-653f9a28abce",
                                "text": "On the Lincolnshire side of the Humber, the Pier Station at New Holland was put out of action when the ferry boat plying to and from Hull broke loose from its moorings."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ade201c7-20fb-48af-884f-13a2206e5830",
                                "sense_id": "081f8fd9-3c03-3f3a-ab68-653f9a28abce",
                                "text": "On the opposite wall, the R101 tragedy is recalled by the airship's tattered ensign in a glass case, a plaque from the Royal Airship Works and a photograph of the dirigible at her moorings."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "56697edf-8376-3916-8ccc-fff5d0a1bd5d",
                        "entry_id": "ab3a14b4-ad67-34fa-b670-1cbac7d84385",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act of securing a vessel with a cable or anchor etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "500f4183-2bd8-3247-9907-44a9a153d1aa",
                        "entry_id": "ab3a14b4-ad67-34fa-b670-1cbac7d84385",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Something to which one adheres, or the means that helps one to maintain a stable position and keep one's identity - moral, intellectual, political, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fadc672d-1e5b-4d72-83d4-ce5fcfb797c6",
                                "sense_id": "500f4183-2bd8-3247-9907-44a9a153d1aa",
                                "text": "1890, John George Nicolay and John Hay, Abraham Lincoln: A History\nThe party of pro-slavery reaction was for the moment in the ascendant; and as by an irresistible impulse, the Supreme Court of the United States was swept from its hitherto impartial judicial moorings into the dangerous seas of polities."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "777edb83-2c19-4f89-b42f-1b68444b381d",
                                "sense_id": "500f4183-2bd8-3247-9907-44a9a153d1aa",
                                "text": "1898, Coates, Florence Earle, song: \"Friendship from its Moorings Strays\"\nFriendship from its moorings strays,\nLove binds fast together;\nFriendship is for balmy days,\nLove for stormy weather."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8adf1663-725a-437a-b08e-bc2de0e7ba0e",
                        "source_entry_id": "ab3a14b4-ad67-34fa-b670-1cbac7d84385",
                        "source_sense_description": "place to moor a vessel",
                        "target_lang_word": "bitte",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bitte",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fe5d872-deda-3a0d-a304-c79da39befb9",
                                        "entry_id": "b8a75033-2651-3c9a-9c8a-c1147412c3e1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pièce verticale, de section ronde ou carrée, que l’on trouve sur le quai d’un port et que l’on utilise pour amarrer les bateaux."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea4488eb-e130-496d-b49f-cde649f6bffd",
                                                "sense_id": "7fe5d872-deda-3a0d-a304-c79da39befb9",
                                                "text": "Assise sur une bitte\n D’amarrage, elle pleure\nSon homme qui la quitte,\n La mer c’est son malheur."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7f3ee9e-a2b4-49e5-8f34-cfc7e19ccc78",
                                                "sense_id": "7fe5d872-deda-3a0d-a304-c79da39befb9",
                                                "text": "Je suis encore restée quelque temps à regarder les ondulations du canal Saint-George, la ligne granitique des quais, la tension des cordages, la rigidité des bittes – un des premiers mots français dont Monsieur Presle m’ait appris le sens à cause de ses origines scandinaves : « biti, poutre transversale de navire »."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80aab79a-d66c-455a-bd7b-704cf08341bc",
                                                "sense_id": "7fe5d872-deda-3a0d-a304-c79da39befb9",
                                                "text": "La bitte d’amarrage est alors enfoncée dans le béton frais de manière à laisser environ 300 mm de tube exposé."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0ea6e252-755d-34b6-ab12-9708dec9449a",
                                        "entry_id": "b8a75033-2651-3c9a-9c8a-c1147412c3e1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Variante orthographique de bite."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b5d5eaf-bbbd-40f0-b95c-b930a7c1e5a8",
                                                "sense_id": "0ea6e252-755d-34b6-ab12-9708dec9449a",
                                                "text": "Évidemment, on pouvait être sûr qu’elle avait vu plus d’une bitte."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
